DECISION
AR-H134 is POSITIVE
for:
FIT-GATED REPRESENTATION-DEBT FAMILY COMPACTION

WITH:
A FALSE-CLUSTERING LIMIT.

Supported synthetically:

- cheap residual markers still create aggregate memory pressure;
- age pruning loses large future recall;
- current-frequency pruning is worse under rare recurrence;
- debt-family clustering greatly reduces storage;
- fit-gated compaction preserves most future target recall;
- aggressive clustering creates false-cause contamination;
- representation debt can itself be organized as a developmental family ecology.

Not demonstrated:

- online family split/merge under many context shifts;
- family-level re-audition scheduling;
- hierarchical debt families;
- residual-provenance corruption;
- debt-family interaction with hypothesis birth;
- real representation reconstruction.

